      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_001",
      "unit_text": "Good evening from Hofstra University in Hempstead, New York.",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 60,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Moderator greeting",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_001",
      "turn_index": 0,
      "speaker_id": "spk_001",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_002",
      "unit_text": "We begin tonight with the central question of jobs and trade",
      "char_start": 61,
      "char_end": 121,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Moderator topic setting",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_001",
      "turn_index": 0,
      "speaker_id": "spk_001",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_003",
      "unit_text": "how each candidate plans to achieve broad-based prosperity for American workers.",
      "char_start": 127,
      "char_end": 207,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Moderator question framing",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_001",
      "turn_index": 0,
      "speaker_id": "spk_001",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_004",
      "unit_text": "Secretary Clinton, you have two minutes to begin.",
      "char_start": 208,
      "char_end": 257,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Moderator floor assignment",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_005",
      "unit_text": "Thank you, Lester.",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 18,
      "component_label": "OTHER",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Salutation",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_006",
      "unit_text": "We have to build an economy that works for everyone, not just those at the top.",
      "char_start": 19,
      "char_end": 98,
      "component_label": "CLAIM",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Central economic vision",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_007",
      "unit_text": "That means creating good-paying jobs by investing in renewable energy, modernizing our electrical grid",
      "char_start": 99,
      "char_end": 201,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Renewable investment rationale",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_008",
      "unit_text": "raising the federal minimum wage to guarantee fair pay for honest labor.",
      "char_start": 207,
      "char_end": 279,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Wage floor rationale",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_009",
      "unit_text": "Independent nonpartisan economic evaluations show that our public investment proposal will produce over ten million new jobs across the next five years.",
      "char_start": 280,
      "char_end": 432,
      "component_label": "EVIDENCE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Independent study citing 10 million jobs",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_002",
      "turn_index": 1,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_010",
      "unit_text": "We must also guarantee paid family leave so working parents do not face financial ruin simply for caring for a newborn child or an ailing parent.",
      "char_start": 433,
      "char_end": 578,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "note": "Subordinate premise illustrating family welfare",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_003",
      "turn_index": 2,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_011",
      "unit_text": "Our jobs are fleeing our country",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 32,
      "component_label": "CLAIM",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Main thesis on jobs fleeing",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_003",
      "turn_index": 2,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_012",
      "unit_text": "bad trade deals are the single greatest cause of our manufacturing decline.",
      "char_start": 38,
      "char_end": 113,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Causal premise on bad trade deals",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_003",
      "turn_index": 2,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_013",
      "unit_text": "For twenty years, agreements like NAFTA have drained American industrial capability, sending thousands of manufacturing facilities to Mexico and allowing China to devalue its currency without repercussion.",
      "char_start": 114,
      "char_end": 319,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "note": "Historical explanation of NAFTA impact",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_003",
      "turn_index": 2,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_014",
      "unit_text": "Look at states like Ohio, Michigan",
      "char_start": 320,
      "char_end": 354,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "note": "Geographic examples of industrial decline",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_003",
      "turn_index": 2,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_015",
      "unit_text": "Pennsylvania, where over five million manufacturing jobs have vanished since the turn of the century.",
      "char_start": 360,
      "char_end": 461,
      "component_label": "EVIDENCE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "5M jobs lost data",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_003",
      "turn_index": 2,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_016",
      "unit_text": "We must stop our companies from leaving by drastically cutting our corporate tax rate from thirty-five percent down to fifteen percent and renegotiating these disastrous trade agreements.",
      "char_start": 462,
      "char_end": 649,
      "component_label": "CLAIM",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Tax reform policy claim",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_004",
      "turn_index": 3,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_017",
      "unit_text": "Donald, your plan would implement the most extreme version of trickle-down economics in modern American history.",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 112,
      "component_label": "COUNTERARGUMENT",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Attack on trickle-down framing",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_004",
      "turn_index": 3,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_018",
      "unit_text": "Independent analysts at the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget confirmed that your tax proposal would add five trillion dollars to the national debt while directing the vast majority of tax relief to multi-millionaires.",
      "char_start": 113,
      "char_end": 340,
      "component_label": "EVIDENCE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "CRFB report citation",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_004",
      "turn_index": 3,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_019",
      "unit_text": "We tried trickle-down policies in 2008 and it resulted in the Great Recession, wiping out nine million jobs and five trillion dollars in household wealth.",
      "char_start": 341,
      "char_end": 495,
      "component_label": "EVIDENCE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "2008 recession figures",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_004",
      "turn_index": 3,
      "speaker_id": "spk_002",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_020",
      "unit_text": "What we need is investment from the middle out and the ground up, not another failed round of unpaid tax breaks for the wealthy.",
      "char_start": 496,
      "char_end": 624,
      "component_label": "CLAIM",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "note": "Stand-alone policy principle for middle-out growth",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_005",
      "turn_index": 4,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_021",
      "unit_text": "That five trillion dollar estimate is completely incorrect because it assumes static economic growth rather than the dynamic expansion our tax reform will unleash.",
      "char_start": 0,
      "char_end": 163,
      "component_label": "REBUTTAL",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "note": "Direct refutation of static scoring",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_005",
      "turn_index": 4,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_022",
      "unit_text": "When we reduce the regulatory burden and cut corporate taxes to fifteen percent, trillions of dollars currently held overseas will repatriate directly into American factories and machinery.",
      "char_start": 164,
      "char_end": 353,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Repatriation explanation",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "debate_id": "debate_002_us2016",
      "source_corpus": "us2016",
      "source_license": "UNVERIFIED",
      "turn_id": "turn_005",
      "turn_index": 4,
      "speaker_id": "spk_003",
      "speaker_role": "Debater",
      "speaker_side": "Neutral",
      "unit_id": "u_023",
      "unit_text": "We will bring back our manufacturing base because companies will finally have a compelling economic incentive to build and hire right here in the United States.",
      "char_start": 354,
      "char_end": 514,
      "component_label": "PREMISE",
      "annotator_id": "annotator_B",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "Corporate hiring rationale",
      "guideline_version": "1.0.0"
    }
